extraction_notes: "WB17 Warlords of Russia printed 66-69 (cache p067-p070, cache page = printed folio + 1), read off the text layer. Heading The Huntsman-Trapper O.C.C. at the top of printed 66; the special abilities are printed 66-68 and the stat block headed The Russian Huntsman-Trapper O.C.C. (also known as Woodsman and Trapper) starts on printed 68. The entry ends on printed 69, where its Note, Money and Cybernetics lines are interleaved in the text layer with the opening of the Travelling Story Teller (cache p070 lines 57-80 are the Huntsman''s). || GROUP: listed under Russian Adventurer O.C.C.s on printed 57; the entry states no S.D.C. base, so men_of_arms is false and occ_group is optional. || XP: the Huntsman-Trapper ladder on the Experience Tables, printed 6, read off a render; the book misprints level 5 as 18,501, level 4 ends at 16,500, so 16501 is stored. || BONUSES: +2 initiative, +3 pull punch, +3 vs possession stored flat; +1 to save vs magic is stored as spell_magic only (a reading: the book says magic, not spell or ritual); +2 vs poison and disease is stored as toxins_poisons 2 and disease 2; +1 vs Horror Factor at levels 1, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 10, 12 and 14 is stored as horror_factor 1 flat for level 1 plus eight at_level entries. || P.P.E.: 4D6 + P.E. attribute number and +1D4 per level, stored in ppe_base and repeated as a special ability. || SPECIAL ABILITIES: the three percentile abilities (Track and Trap 20%/30% +5%, Recognize Supernatural Shapechangers 30% +5%, Forest-wise 20% +4%) are special_abilities prose. Track & Trap Animals is ALSO stored as an occ skill at 20/5 because the catalog holds a row of that name at the same figures; that is a reading, and the 30% trapping number lives only in its note. Recognize Supernatural Shapechangers and Forest-wise have no catalog skill row. The Code of the Huntsman-Trapper (printed 68) is stored as a special ability, paraphrased. || SKILLS NOT STORED: Lore: Geomancy & Ley Lines (+10%) has no catalog row and is left out. Speaks Faerie has no catalog language row; it is stored as one of three Language: Other picks at +10%. || SKILL READINGS: Lore: Faeries is the catalog''s Lore: Faeries & Creatures of Magic; Identify Plants & Fruits is Identify Plants & Fruit; Tracking is Tracking (people); Advanced Math is Mathematics: Advanced. Falconry is filed under Military in the catalog, so Military appears with only Falconry at the +15% the book prints under Technical, although the book says Military: None; Whittling at +15% is not stored (Technical is a flat +10). Prowl is filed under Physical and is reached by name through the Rogue only-list at +10%. Pilot: any, except robots, power armor, military vehicles, ships and aircraft is read as excluding ALL ships and aircraft (the Explorer on printed 65 says military aircraft; this entry does not); Horsemanship is its own catalog category and is offered as General and Exotic Animals only, on the Vehicle line''s remark that a Huntsman may know how to ride a horse. Hand to Hand: Expert, no others available, is costs: {}. || MONEY: the book prints no coin: 4D4x100 credits WORTH of furs, horns, bone, nuggets of silver or gold and other tradeable goods (the text layer prints 4D4xlOO). starting_money is 0 and the goods are in GM Notes. || EQUIPMENT not stored as rows: one weapon for each W.P.; skinning knives, flint and tinder box, cooking utensils, frying pan, a box of 100 plastic sandwich bags, a box of 100 large bags, 1D4 airtight plastic containers, bedroll, belt, boots, fur cloak or long coat, note pad, 20 feet of wire and personal items have no catalog row and are in GM Notes. The text layer prints scalable for sealable. The armor is stored as the light homemade suit; the lore text on printed 67 says such armor is typically 30-60 M.D.C. and rarely environmental. || NOT STORED: Secret Resources and the Note on how Reavers, War Camp soldiers, Bogatyrs, Demon Hunters and Ectohunters regard the class are in GM Notes; only 15% have partial bionics (printed 67)."
---

## Lore

The Huntsman-Trapper is part hunter, part trapper and part forest guide: a
burly, loud, cheerfully crude woodsman who lives by his own code in the deep
Russian forests where even War-Knights hesitate to go. City folk take him for
a dim barbarian. He is nothing of the kind; surviving out there takes
alertness, invention and cunning, and most Huntsmen read people as well as
they read tracks.

Villages hire them to deal with man-killers, livestock thieves and things far
worse, and to find people lost or taken in the woods. A Huntsman does not just
go and kill the problem. He spends a few days studying the creature and the
community, and often ends it by relocating an animal, building a fence, or
striking a bargain with Faerie Folk, werebeasts or woodland spirits, who treat
him as one of their own. Man-eaters and truly evil supernatural beings get no
such bargain.

They wear patchwork armor of hide, bone and scavenged plate, favor
Vibro-Blades and heavy energy weapons, and mostly shun bionics.

## GM Notes

Percentile abilities the sheet does not roll for you: Track and Trap is 20%
tracking / 30% trapping, +5% per level (tracking humans at -20%, disarming
traps meant for humans at half); Recognize Supernatural Shapechangers is 30%
+5% per level; Forest-wise is 20% +4% per level.

The save vs Horror Factor rises by +1 at levels 1, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 10, 12
and 14.

One of the three language picks is Faerie. The book also grants Lore:
Geomancy & Ley Lines (+10%), which the catalog does not hold.

Starting kit beyond what the sheet lists: one weapon for each W.P. with 1D4+2
extra clips apiece, skinning knives, flint and tinder box, cooking utensils,
frying pan, a box of 100 plastic sandwich bags, a box of 100 large sealable
bags, 1D4 airtight plastic containers, bedroll, belt, boots, a fur cloak or
long coat, note pad, 20 feet (6 m) of wire and a handful of personal items.

Money: no coin. The Huntsman starts with 4D4x100 credits worth of furs, horns,
bone, nuggets of silver or gold and other tradeable goods (herbs, spices,
birds, small animals).

Secret resources: none as such, but Huntsmen are highly regarded by Gypsies,
Travelling Story Tellers, Mystic Kuznya, Mega-Horses and peasants. Reavers and
War Camp soldiers dislike, envy and somewhat fear them, and often bully and
harass them, yet turn to them for woodland expertise. Bogatyrs and Demon
Hunters usually like them; Ectohunters tend to see them as crude rivals.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'huntsman-trapper');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'huntsman-trapper';

